## Sanitizer policy

|| Model     | Parameter          | Action                                                                                                                                                             ||
|| --------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ ||
|| `glm-5.3` | `thinking`         | Always `{type: "enabled"}` — `disabled` is **not supported** and fails upstream                                                                                    ||
|| `glm-5.3` | `reasoning_effort` | Always sent, `low`\|`high`\|`max`. Normalized via `normalizeZaiEffort()` → `off`/`none`/`minimal`↦`low`, `medium`↦`high`, `xhigh`↦`max`, `high`/`max` pass-through ||
|| `glm-4.7` | `thinking`         | Set `{type: "enabled"\|"disabled"}` (toggle, live `ThinkingEnabled` map); no reasoning_effort support                                                              ||
|| `glm-4.7` | `reasoning_effort` | Deleted                                                                                                                                                            ||

The thinking-toggle set is a whitelist (`zaiThinkingToggle()`): `glm-4.7` only.
Apply `PolicyZai` case in `applyThinkingPolicy()` and `stripUnsupportedParams()`.

## Reasoning effort normalization (Z.AI-specific)

`glm-5.3` always thinks — thinking cannot be disabled upstream, so the minimum
effort level is `low`. The gateway normalizes effort via `normalizeZaiEffort()`
to the values the catalog advertises (`low`, `high`, `max` are ever sent):

|| UI label    | Sent to Z.AI                                         ||
|| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------- ||
|| Off / None  | `low` (minimum thinking — `disabled` is unsupported) ||
|| Low         | `low`                                                ||
|| Medium      | `high`                                               ||
|| High        | `high`                                               ||
|| XHigh / Max | `max`                                                ||

The `ReasoningEffortCatalog` entry for `glm-5.3` advertises: `low`, `high`, `max`
and defaults to `low` (cost-conscious, mirroring Kimi K3).
`glm-4.7` does not appear in the catalog (no effort selection).

