## Plan concurrency (capacity model)

`glm-4.7` (and the whole GLM Coding Plan) allows ~2 concurrent requests.
The gateway enforces ONE shared budget (`zaiSem`, cap 2) across every
coding-plan client — chat, router downgrades, and the `glm-4.6v` vision
worker. When the budget is full:

- **Direct glm-4.7/glm-5.3**: ~2s grace wait, then **overflow** to
  `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731` (OpenRouter) via
  `acquireZaiLaneOrOverflow`.
- **Router downgrades**: non-blocking, overflow immediately via
  `selectDowngradeLane`.
- **Vision**: blocks on `zaiSem` (chat yields first).

Never queue on glm-4.7 when a fast lane exists — queueing is the perceived
slowness. Overflow policy lives in `internal/gateway/fallback.go`.

