## Balance API

Z.AI is credits-based (GLM Coding Plan). The usage dashboard fetches remaining
credits via the quota API:
- `GET https://api.z.ai/api/monitor/usage/quota/limit` (Bearer auth, returns `data.limits[]` buckets of type `CREDIT_LIMIT` with `remaining`/`percentage`). The weekly bucket carries a `nextResetTime`; the 5-hour bucket does not.

Also checkable manually at https://z.ai/manage-apikey/billing.

GLM-5.3 Coding Plan usage is **points-based** (2026-08): credits are consumed by
token multipliers per 10k tokens — input 6.9, cached input 1.7, output 24 —
split by peak/off-peak (off-peak = 50% of standard). The dashboard balance
panel parses whatever `data.limits[]` buckets arrive, so no code change is
required to display the new quota.

Coding Plan tiers (2026-08): **Lite** = 2,000 / 5-hour, 10,000 / weekly;
**Pro** = 12,000 / 5-hour, 60,000 / weekly (6x Lite). The user is on **Pro**
($64/mo effective committed — 3 months upfront on an $80/mo list plan).
`ZaiFlatFeeUSD` (Go) = `$64.00` and feeds the month-projection headline and the
`/api/zai-flat-fee` endpoint; it is **not** used for per-token pricing estimates.

## Symptoms & fixes

### `GLM-4.7 feels extremely slow when used in more than one place`

|| Symptom | Cause | Fix ||
|| ------- | ----- | ---- ||
|| GLM-4.7 (or glm-5.3) turns take 20-45s when the main chat + parallel subagents all use it | Coding-plan concurrency is ~2; excess requests **queue inside the gateway** (or 429 upstream) instead of overflowing to a fast model. A queued glm-4.7 request is far slower than a ~2s cached deepseek-v4-flash turn. | One shared `zaiSem` (cap 2) budgets ALL coding-plan traffic. Direct requests use `acquireZaiLaneOrOverflow` (2s grace, then overflow to deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731). Buy = don't queue: keep glm-4.7 for the 2 highest-value concurrent turns only. ||

